insert into knowledge_chunks (source_file, content, embedding) values ($kc$heat_stress_crop_thresholds.txt$kc$, $kc$For wheat, the critical heat stress threshold during the grain-filling period is generally accepted as a daily maximum above 30°C or a mean temperature above 25°C. At temperatures exceeding 35°C during anthesis (flowering), pollen viability drops sharply — pollen grains desiccate in hot dry air, and fertilisation fails even if photosynthesis is intact. Each degree of mean temperature above 25°C during grain fill reduces wheat yield by approximately 3–8% depending on variety and water availability. In the Indo-Gangetic Plain, late-sown wheat (December planting or later) is particularly exposed to terminal heat stress in March–April when grain is developing.$kc$, '[-0.009424,-0.001255,0.040517,-0.002571,0.063597,0.032962,0.043972,0.000979,-0.035461,-0.055838,-0.013890,-0.108879,0.057996,0.034525,0.012686,0.034922,0.005279,0.024963,-0.028958,-0.002543,0.083454,-0.014335,-0.022437,-0.085105,0.011475,0.041832,-0.039520,0.007594,-0.034128,-0.199635,0.008881,-0.007991,0.041313,-0.035411,-0.034116,-0.062695,-0.022527,0.011265,-0.010425,0.054821,0.048307,0.003806,0.002624,-0.043717,-0.066302,-0.031730,-0.026490,0.007636,0.034960,-0.026540,0.017645,-0.035969,0.035796,0.023320,-0.001515,0.055956,0.053919,0.031631,0.036271,0.031652,-0.016589,0.017029,-0.221358,0.020502,0.067285,-0.005588,0.005892,-0.035494,-0.020244,0.006611,-0.031468,0.056035,0.021363,0.056882,-0.018105,-0.020617,-0.030229,-0.069983,0.027925,0.005840,-0.006683,-0.030260,-0.004143,-0.036653,-0.024117,-0.077700,0.009989,-0.039558,0.028172,-0.036881,-0.032662,-0.034878,-0.041540,0.002021,-0.074351,0.064703,0.019958,-0.031345,-0.053700,0.247782,-0.110873,-0.002667,-0.012288,0.016782,-0.008274,-0.016800,-0.013175,-0.029148,-0.037468,0.033736,0.017325,-0.003691,0.030871,0.036828,0.042667,-0.019836,0.091708,0.024678,-0.024411,0.058190,0.026377,0.039445,0.020887,0.003152,0.033553,-0.035811,0.011229,0.121