insert into knowledge_chunks (source_file, content, embedding) values ($kc$heat_stress_crop_thresholds.txt$kc$, $kc$For rice, heat stress thresholds differ by stage. During the pollination and early grain fill stage (usually around heading), sustained daytime temperatures above 35°C impair pollen germination on the stigma, leading to sterile spikelets and yield loss. Night-time temperatures are also critical for rice: nights above 26°C increase dark respiration, burning photosynthate that would otherwise accumulate as grain starch. Research in tropical Asia suggests each 1°C increase in minimum night temperature reduces rice yields by 6–10%. Kharif (monsoon) rice in India is increasingly exposed to high night temperatures due to warming trends.$kc$, '[-0.025624,0.016921,0.067801,-0.001356,0.091000,0.060026,0.071462,0.010175,-0.017014,-0.050553,0.004774,-0.064046,0.038662,0.051208,0.019561,0.011764,0.014023,-0.015379,-0.014587,-0.020583,0.072052,-0.027020,0.005899,-0.090254,0.027048,0.022207,-0.033426,-0.014127,-0.059987,-0.221468,0.012457,-0.013849,-0.005744,-0.011046,-0.031392,-0.032319,-0.038202,0.009985,-0.011099,0.030244,0.066854,-0.036629,0.022267,-0.056582,-0.069899,-0.043354,-0.041074,0.020766,0.035003,-0.015453,0.013947,-0.034505,0.018798,0.026686,-0.005450,-0.003699,0.108876,0.089360,0.059575,0.062654,0.020629,0.066960,-0.214398,0.041800,0.041116,-0.006277,-0.028283,-0.006502,-0.001236,0.004754,-0.049677,0.062196,0.003916,0.035280,-0.004911,-0.063506,-0.005915,-0.054411,-0.000452,0.023840,-0.000688,-0.035493,-0.010525,-0.022375,-0.020726,-0.031840,0.017212,-0.066192,0.001201,-0.010385,-0.009864,-0.075129,-0.054840,-0.023713,-0.064115,0.023280,0.026842,-0.018519,-0.044092,0.227648,-0.040847,0.031183,0.011635,0.015268,-0.003113,-0.054783,-0.028286,-0.007560,-0.035267,0.050153,0.033053,-0.006081,0.014188,0.024916,0.059574,-0.008559,0.085582,0.024957,-0.029665,0.041599,0.009712,0.040241,0.058610,-0.045212,0.014626,-0.061683,-0.032526,0.116125,0.039046,-0.018263