insert into knowledge_chunks (source_file, content, embedding) values ($kc$rainfall_variability_climate_change.txt$kc$, $kc$In South Asia and many tropical regions, climate change is not simply reducing total rainfall — it is making it more erratic. Research shows that while some regions are seeing modest increases in annual precipitation totals, the same rainfall is often delivered in fewer, more intense events with longer dry intervals in between. This "drying on the margins, wetting in the extremes" pattern creates twin problems: waterlogging stress from intense rain events and moisture stress during extended dry spells within the same season.$kc$, '[0.005415,-0.014151,0.084886,0.029074,0.050299,-0.001681,0.023317,0.009016,0.025619,-0.011591,-0.001173,-0.066092,0.083495,0.030750,0.026914,-0.006744,0.005587,0.000704,-0.052769,0.010451,0.023471,0.029049,0.007938,-0.081335,0.015081,0.031867,-0.017838,-0.021381,-0.019564,-0.235423,0.016600,-0.004737,-0.012373,-0.019854,-0.017827,-0.039751,-0.018597,0.058623,0.004131,0.015832,0.018698,0.023238,-0.000963,-0.082615,-0.069903,-0.047264,-0.003883,0.035302,0.005207,-0.034156,0.011028,-0.016457,0.016606,0.017712,0.017222,0.009690,0.033619,0.075861,0.013114,0.005414,0.023453,0.025667,-0.243271,0.075958,0.086028,-0.001648,-0.058960,-0.007430,0.025230,0.032316,-0.069478,0.051550,0.043674,0.063638,0.038032,-0.008716,-0.057049,0.018663,-0.038058,0.000647,0.018746,-0.042140,-0.051457,-0.041742,-0.025586,-0.070998,-0.000685,-0.068250,0.059757,-0.046713,0.007271,-0.025996,0.023762,0.031986,-0.066425,0.028235,0.019077,0.012411,-0.034095,0.237725,-0.092293,0.026459,0.035682,0.028008,0.023804,-0.018668,-0.034151,-0.082076,-0.014165,0.007466,0.008035,-0.019704,0.039360,-0.022007,-0.002572,-0.067839,0.035174,0.042013,-0.025334,0.028736,-0.020533,0.047071,0.037862,-0.023694,0.015212,-0.030775,0.054160,0.095184,0.022410,-0.010341,0.068891,-0.044682,-0.043918,-0.051028,0.006299,-0.023236,0.007179,0.016340,0.011026,-0.022941,-0.040765,-0.04